Asbestosis
Asbestosis is a chronic respiratory condition which, like the name indicates, is directly attributable to asbestos exposure. Asbestosis can cause internal respiratory damage that will seriously limit lung function. Asbestosis has also been known to occur as a precursor to mesothelioma and other malignancies such as lung cancer.
Asbestos Lung Cancer
Lung cancer, which is different than mesothelioma because it actually occurs in the lung tissue as opposed to the mesothelium, can also be attributed to asbestos exposure. There are general sub-classifications of lung cancer. These are and which are assigned based on how the cancer cells appear within the lung tissue. Each of these types has appeared in those exposed to asbestos.",1
