"Botswana is the world's most important producer of valuable diamonds. De Beers has had a special relationship with Botswana since 1987 when Botswana sold its diamond stockpile to De Beers for 250 million dollars and a 5.27 percent share in the company. The contract between Botswana and De Beers expired on December 31, 1990. A new contract is being negotiated, and Botswana wants to sell some of its output independently. De Beers rejects that. Argyle Diamonds of Australia is also negotiating a new contract with De Beers. Australia ranks first in volume of diamonds produced, but only sixth in terms of value.","!
